    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0258" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/969A.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Ambassador
                        to Great Britain</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-26T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 26, 1912—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Informally inquire what attitude is likely to be taken by the Foreign Office
                    toward the loan negotiations now proceeding at Peking; especially whether some
                    steps will not be taken to insure the further advances that may be needed by
                    China while the negotiations are in progress.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Berlin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
